message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Did renewables actually displace fossil power? A reproducible cross-country analysis, 2000-2022"
authors:
  - family-names: "Your Name"
    given-names: ""
    orcid: "0000-0000-0000-0000"   # replace with your ORCID
date-released: 2026-09-11
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://github.com/your-github-username/renewables-vs-fossil"
repository-code: "https://github.com/your-github-username/renewables-vs-fossil"
abstract: >-
  We test whether a rising renewable-electricity share displaced fossil generation
  across 187 countries (2000-2022). With country- and year-fixed-effects models plus
  generation-level accounting, we find decoupling of carbon intensity is real, yet
  absolute fossil generation rose in roughly 70% of countries. We quantify the 2030
  low-carbon deployment rate required merely to hold fossil generation flat.
